      "message": "fix(post): a left-hand cutter posts M4 or refuses - never M3\n\nThe rework of PR #4103 after mkinney''s review, four items:\n\n- the cutter-hand law now reads the REQUEST, not the post: a\n  left-hand cutter is refused by name for every operation that does\n  not ask the spindle to reverse (today only a Thread operation with\n  spindle reverse), and still refused on the M3-only posts even then;\n  a permitted post reverses nothing on its own, and a user post file\n  is judged by the same request (tool_gate: tool_refusal,\n  tool_problem, the generation and post doors);\n- output tests: the Thread op with the ask posts M4; the whole\n  catalog table of kinds refuses the left hand without the ask; the\n  Drill refuses on the reversing Fanuc as much as on Haas, with no\n  NC file written;\n- examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj regenerated at v83\n  through the WRITE_GOLDEN save path; the committed program is\n  unchanged;\n- the library-version boundary test refuses CUTTER_HAND_VERSION + 1\n  (the new newest version), not TIP_FORM_VERSION + 1.\n\nFixes #4031",
